## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **My first F2 verification (T2)** — failed because: the temp PLANET.md was written with `Set-Content -Encoding utf8`, which in PowerShell 5.1 adds a **UTF-8 BOM**; the BOM before `##` defeated the hook's `^` anchor → regex didn't match → false exit 0. Fix was in the TEST (write no-BOM via `.NET UTF8Encoding($false)`) AND defensively in the hook (strip leading BOM) — the real PLANET.md has no BOM, but Windows editors add them silently.
- **`Measure-Object -Line` for NORTH_STAR line count** — failed/misled: returned 48, I used it to wrongly dismiss the audit's correct finding that the file is ~65 lines. Direct `Read` showed 65. Lesson: verify the auditor, but don't trust a single quick measurement over a direct read.
- **Inline `node -e` with a Windows path in backtick-quoted PS string** — failed because: PowerShell backtick is an escape char, mangled the path. Fixed by passing the path as `process.argv[1]`.
- **`Remove-Item C:\_hooktest -Recurse -Force`** — blocked by a sandbox guard ("system path 'A:' blocked" — a false match). Worked around by not calling Remove-Item; temp dirs `C:\_hooktest`, `C:\_hooktest2` left on disk (harmless junk, can delete manually).
- **The "mechanism not discipline / can't die again" claim in commit `99ea6d11`** — was FALSE when made: the staleness hook still only read PLAN.md (prose changed, not code). Caught by the fresh-eyes audit; fixed in `5956c67a`.

